  "title": "Frozen means fixed height, and untouched sides beyond a cut collapse",
  "subject": "Which points a port pattern freezes, and why the halo left the faces around the attachment point at a junction",
  "conclusion": "A port pattern freezes exactly the points whose height difference to the ports cannot vary, and a side beyond a 3-edge cut that holds neither the handle nor the gluing line can be collapsed to the vertex it lost without changing creation. In the collapsed space the halo again lies on the faces around the attachment point, so a ring spliced onto a grid shows the full ladder halo along its far face.",
